  "summary": "The ranked studies apply representation learning with paired positive and negative examples to the task of estimating battery remaining life. The reported performance varies across datasets, with Chen et al. (2019) achieving 0.75 accuracy on GridWatch [V0095], Brennan et al. (2018) reporting an F1 score of 0.68 on ToxiBench [V0094], and Adebayo et al. (2026) obtaining a 0.61 AUROC on CellLife [V0093]. Duarte et al. (2020) also apply this method on ProtMap, reporting an MAE of 0.82 [V0096].",
